  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Addressing Urgent Needs in Iraq: Screening, Rehabilitation, and Reintegration of Adults, Management of High-Risk Prisoners, and Protection Needs of Children Returned from Syria (the &#x201c;Activities&#x201d;)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will support the Government of Iraq (GoI) in managing individuals returned from Syria and ensure effective ownership of the process until the all-of-UN program of support is developed under the Global Framework and a dedicated multi-partner trust fund mechanism is established. Given the urgent need to support security and accountability and address the protection needs of children, this project will support the GoI to (i) Manage suspected foreign terrorist fighters (FTF) and violent extremist prisoners (VEP) (ii) Address the urgent rehabilitation and reintegration needs of current and future returnees as well as VEPs; (iii) Address the urgent protection needs of current and future returnee children, as well as foreign children still detained in Iraq for alleged affiliation with the Islamic State in Iraq and the Levant (ISIL) and (iv) Ensure effective ownership of the return, rehabilitation, and reintegration process.</narrative>
  </description>
